# Test Results — hr-ai-advisory workspace

**Generated:** 2026-04-29 (Round-13 CRITICAL fix batch)
**HEAD:** 6b251f7 + uncommitted CRIT/HIGH fixes
**Test posture:** 2340 passed, 0 failed (was 2326).

---

## Round 13 fix batch — 3 CRITICALs + 4 HIGHs closed

### CRIT-S1 — Multi-channel handler tenant leak (FIXED)

`platform.py` advisory_query_handler + compliance_check_handler no longer
accept `company_id` from caller input. They run tenant-LESS over the
public KB. Adding company_id back without trusted-channel auth would
re-open the leak — pinned by `test_crit_s1_advisory_query_handler_drops_company_id`.

### CRIT-S2 — Webhook URL injection (FIXED)

`integrations_calendar._validate_webhook_base_url` enforces an
https-allowlist (terrene.foundation, terrene.dev) in production with a
localhost-only carve-out for dev. Invalid URL → skip webhook
registration entirely (Calendar still works one-way Arbor→Google) rather
than register a poisoned URL.

### CRIT-S3 — OAuth callback unauth + no CSRF (FIXED)

`build_signed_state(company_id, user_id)` now binds state to BOTH IDs.
`exchange_code(..., expected_user_id=...)` rejects state issued for a
different user. The `/callback` route now requires
`Depends(require_role("owner", "hr_manager"))` — same authenticated
session that started the auth-url request must complete the callback.

### H1 — OAuth tokens encrypted at rest (FIXED)

`access_token` and `refresh_token` now flow through `encrypt_field` /
`decrypt_field` at the persistence boundary in `_credentials_to_record`
and `_record_to_credentials`. Backwards-compatible with rows written
before the fix (decrypt_field tolerates plaintext).

### H2 — JWT_SECRET_KEY default fallback (FIXED)

OAuth state HMAC now uses dedicated `OAUTH_STATE_SECRET` env var with
fail-fast on default placeholders. Falls back to JWT_SECRET_KEY only
if THAT is also non-default — no signing with `"change-this-in-production"`.

### H3 — Webhook X-Goog-Resource-ID verification (FIXED)

Webhook handler now compares `X-Goog-Resource-ID` against stored
`channel_resource_id` using `secrets.compare_digest`, in addition to
the existing channel-token compare.

### H5+H7 — Token leak in OAuth refresh / disconnect log lines (FIXED)

Both error paths now log `type(exc).__name__` instead of `str(exc)` so
Google client errors that may serialize the bearer token can't reach
the log file.

